The City reported, among others, the following significant accomplishments in CY 2021:
a. Coronavirus Disease 2019 (COVID-19) Response:
Provided 55 vaccination sites and vaccinated over 3 million individuals;
Provided 22-bed Capacity for emergency services - COVID-19 modular and 60-bed capacity COVID-19 ward in Ospital ng Maynila Medical Center;
Provided new COVID-19 ward and 3-bed capacity intensive care unit room in Ospital ng Tondo;
Provided COVID-19 ward with intensive care capabilities in Ospital ng Sampaloc;
Purchased 12 freezers as storage for COVID-19 vaccines at Manila COVID-19 Vaccine Facility in Sta. Ana Hospital; and
Converted the San Andres Sports Complex and Canonigo covered court as quarantine facility, vaccination site and temporary shelter for street dwellers.
b. Established the Hearing Loss and Deafness Center in Justice Jose Abad Santos General Hospital;
c. Purchased five properties (Francisco Tan, Chona Dimayuga, Adela Tuason, Beatriz Tuazon and Antonio Samia properties) through the Land-for-the-Landless Program;
d. Installed real time Air Quality Monitoring Station for Asia Blue Skies Program at Barangays 128 and 492, and Dr. Jose Fabella Memorial Hospital;
e. Conducted the Nilad Tree-Planting Activity at ASEAN Garden, Intramuros, Manila;
f. Distributed monthly monetary allowance to 180,678 senior citizens from January to September 2021;
g. Granted P100,000.00 cash gift for 15 centenarians;
h. Construction/ Repair/ rehabilitation/ improvement/ upgrading/ installation of various structures and facilities:
Completion of the following major infrastructure projects:
1. 229 units of two-storey Townhouse at Basecommunity;
2. 344-bed capacity Manila COVID-19 Field Hospital;
3. Sta. Ana Hospital Hemodialysis Center
4. Manila Muslim Cemetery and Cultural Hall;
5. Manila District Traffic Enforcement Unit Headquarters;
6. Perimeter fence at Nursery and Green House of the Manila Boystown Complex;
7. Pasig River Esplanade along Baseco Compound; and
8. Upgrading, concreting and drainage improvement of Conchu Street from P. Ocampo to Estrada Streets.
Ongoing construction of the following projects:
1. 15-storey housing project - Tondominium 1 and 2;
2. 15-storey housing project - Binondominium 1;
3. 10-storey Ospital ng Maynila Medical Center and Parking Building;
4. Three-storey community hospital at Baseco Compound;
5. 10-Storey Dr. Albert Elementary School;
6. 10-Storey Rosauro Almario Elementary School;
7. 10-Storey Manila Science High School; and
8. San Sebastian Residences, Pedro Gil Residences and San Lazaro Residences.
Ongoing redevelopment of five-hectare Manila Zoological and Botanical Garden;
Rehabilitation and redevelopment of sports complexes, parks, playgrounds and skate parks;
Installation of 9,072 LED solar-powered road studs and 75,039 square meters new asphalt road pavement;
Installation/repair/relamping/rewiring of 1,032 streetlights;
Refurbished/maintained 27 parks and completed 22,000 square meters urban greening projects; and
Bundling of wires and cable operations on 95 major streets.
In the same year, the City received the following awards/recognitions during the year:
City and Municipalities Competitiveness Index 2021
For Highly Urbanized Cities Category:
2nd Place - Overall Competitiveness Award
1st Place - Most Competitive in Government Efficiency Award
1st Place - Most Competitive in Infrastructure Award
10th Digital Governance Award 2021
1st Place - Best in Customer Empowerment - “Connection for Inclusion”
1st Place - Best in LGU Empowerment - Manila COVID-19 Testing Center Web Laboratory Information System
2nd Place - Best in Business Empowerment - GO! Business Permit and Licensing System mobile application
Bloomberg Philanthropies: 2021 Global Mayors Challenge Champion City - Go! Manila mobile application as among the Top 50 Champion Cities
